Selection survives unrelated child output during and after a drag.

VTE pauses PTY reads in start_selection() but Terminal::process() re-arms them
on every tick, and its "deselect if the text under the selection changed"
check compares against the PRIMARY snapshot, which mid-drag is the previous
selection. Under a program that redraws continuously (a spinner rewriting one
line every 32 ms) every mouse selection is cancelled before release, nothing is
copied, and the clipboard silently keeps its earlier content.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/vte/-/issues/2726
          https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/vte/-/issues/2960

--- a/src/vte.cc
+++ b/src/vte.cc
@@ -4051,8 +4051,12 @@
                         scroll_to_bottom();
                 }
                 /* Deselect the current selection if its contents are changed
-                 * by this insertion. */
-                if (!m_selection_resolved.empty()) {
+                 * by this insertion. The reference is the PRIMARY snapshot,
+                 * which is taken at button release: while a drag is still in
+                 * progress it holds the previous selection (or nothing), so
+                 * the comparison is meaningless and would end the drag on the
+                 * first byte of unrelated output. */
+                if (!m_selecting && !m_selection_resolved.empty()) {
                         //FIXMEchpe: this is atrocious
                         auto selection = g_string_new(nullptr);
                         get_selected_text(selection);
@@ -11097,7 +11101,11 @@
                     m_pty_input_source == 0) {
                         m_pty_input_active = false;
                 }
-                connect_pty_read();
+                /* start_selection() paused reading the PTY for the duration
+                 * of the drag; re-arming it here would resume the child's
+                 * output under the pointer. maybe_end_selection() reconnects. */
+                if (!m_selecting)
+                        connect_pty_read();
         }
 
         bool is_active = !m_incoming_queue.empty();
